DIMENSIONS AUTHOR CHECK
Author Check User Guide
Last updated October 2026
Author Check allows you to check researchers for potential research integrity flags based on prior activities, including retractions, unusual networks or productivity. This guide gets you started and walks you through finding a researcher, reading their report, and reviewing the results responsibly.
HOW TO USE THIS GUIDE
* New to Author Check? Start with Section 1, then try Section 2.
* Want to see it done? Look for the navy View the demo boxes. Each links to a short, recorded demo.
* Want the details behind an indicator? See the Author Check Technical Guide for definitions, calculations and data sources.
We highly encourage you to subscribe to product updates at https://updates.dimensions.ai/. Updates will show the most recent changes to the product, which may not be reflected in this document immediately upon release.
AN INDICATOR IS NOT A VERDICT
The indicators in Author Check are not “metrics” that can be used for benchmarking, and none of them can determine misconduct by themself. A highlight means “worth a closer look”, not “this person has done something wrong.”
