SECTION 1  ·  NEW TO AUTHOR CHECK? START HERE.
Getting Started
Author Check helps you spot potential research integrity signals for authors, peer reviewers and editors before you invite, accept or appoint them. It is built around a repeatable four-step workflow.
THE CORE WORKFLOW
1. Find the researcher. Search by name, ORCID, Dimensions Researcher ID, or the DOI of a manuscript to see all of its authors. Go to Section 2.
2. Review the indicators. Open the researcher profile. Anything highlighted in orange is worth a closer look. Go to Section 3.
3. Dig into the details. Review flagged publications and the co-author network to see what sits behind each highlight. Go to Section 3.
4. Export the data. Download the whole profile or individual tables as PDF or CSV. Go to Section 5.


NOTE
Each step feeds the next. A precise search gives you the right profile. A careful read of the indicators tells you where to look. The flagged publications and co-author tables give you the context to decide what, if anything, needs a follow-up.
	BEFORE YOUR FIRST CHECK
* Log in at dimensions.ai and open Author Check from Apps in the left-hand navigation sidebar.
* Have the best identifier you can get. An ORCID or Dimensions Researcher ID gives the quickest and most precise result.
* Skim the Indicators section inside the app so you know what each highlight means.
* Understand that an indicator is not a verdict (see Section 4). Always say in external communications that the data is publicly sourced and does not imply that anyone has done anything wrong.


