	SECTION 2
Finding a Researcher
Open the Researcher Finder to search for one researcher or multiple researchers affiliated with the same institution. You can search by name, ORCID or Dimensions Researcher ID, or you can use a DOI or Dimensions Document ID to return a list of authors.
THREE WAYS TO FIND SOMEONE
Search by
	Best when
	Precision
	Name + affiliation
	You only have a name and, ideally, an institution.
	Good. Several people may share a name, so add an affiliation.
	ORCID or Dimensions Researcher ID
	You have an identifier, for example from a submission system.
	Highest. The quickest and most precise lookup.
	DOI or Dimensions Document ID
	You want to check all the authors listed on one publication.
	Returns every author on that document. A Dimensions Document ID can be for a publication, grant, patent or clinical trial.
	RESEARCHER FINDER FILTERS
STEP 1
Open the filter panel
Click Researcher Finder, then Filter. The filter options appear.
STEP 2
Choose your filters
Select a filter such as Name, ORCID or Affiliation and enter your search. When you use more than one filter, results must match all of them (an “AND” search).
STEP 3
Choose the affiliation scope
If you use Affiliation, set Affiliation filter type to search all known affiliations (past and present) or only the current one, which is the one in the researcher’s Dimensions profile.
STEP 4
Apply Filters
Click Apply filters to execute the search for profiles.
STEP 5
Clear a filter or start over
Clear an individual filter by clicking the “x” at the end of its input. To clear everything, click the Reset link next to Apply filters.


HOW COMBINED FILTERS WORK
Using several filters creates an “AND” search. If you get no results, remove a filter and try again.
