	WHAT THE ORANGE HIGHLIGHTS MEAN
Author Check highlights a researcher in orange when an indicator needs a closer look. Percentile of publication output is never orange.
Indicator
	The question it answers
	Turns orange when
	Percentile of publication output
	How much has this person published compared with their peers?
	Never. Always grey; shown for context only.
	Flagged publications
	Have any of this person’s publications had retractions or other atypical events?
	At least one flagged publication.
	Self-citations
	Does this person ever cite their own or their co-authors’ work?
	No self-citations (with caveats).
	Unusual network flag
	Does this person’s co-author network show unusual patterns?
	The researcher has an unusual network flag.
	Co-authors with network flag
	Do any of their co-authors show unusual network patterns?
	At least one co-author has an unusual network flag.
	Co-authors with flagged publications
	Do their co-authors have flagged publications?
	At least 20% of co-authors have flagged publications.
	

